{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-n0001106","units":[{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"In ΔL, every proper net is canonical.","requires":["ΔL’s definition of a proper net","ΔL’s definition of a canonical net"],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"mechanism","basis":"source","text":"In ΔL, n beta-reductions correspond to n interactions, and this correspondence holds regardless of the order in which the interactions occur.","requires":["Meaning of beta-reduction","Meaning of interaction","Meaning of interaction order"],"citationRequired":true}]}]}
